  <running_head>LYRICA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Addicta quondam progenies Deo</i><br/><i>Sic fudit hostis acrior impios,</i><br/>        <i>Victrixque, dum Moses fidelis</i><br/>        <i>Tendit ad astra manus precantes.</i></p>
    <p><i>Consulta veri quod Sapientia</i><br/><i>Semper minorem Numine te geris,</i><br/>        <i>Regni, vinces, hostibusque</i><br/>        <i>Sceptra feres metuenda cunctis.</i></p>
    <p><i>AEternus orbis nam tibi militat</i><br/><i>Rector, furentes qui quatit improbos,</i><br/>        <i>Virésque vasanas retundit</i><br/>        <i>Omne nefas animo moventes.</i></p>
    <p><i>Quite benigno lumine respicit,</i><br/><i>Tutámque praestat: qui vigil excubat,</i><br/>        <i>Et fraudis authores recludens</i><br/>        <i>Insidias referat latentes.</i></p>
    <p><i>Insanientum te quibus impetit,</i><br/><i>Turbátque liuor Pontificum irritus,</i><br/>        <i>Omnisque coniurata veros</i><br/>        <i>Perdere Christicolas caterua.</i></p>
    <p><i>Te victus auro nunc parat artifex</i><br/><i>Miscere mensis toxica regiis</i><br/>        <i>Maltare, ni tutela Christi</i><br/>        <i>Fraude pium caput expediret.</i></p>
    <p><i>Nunc Iesuites seditionibus</i><br/><i>Paces Britanni vertere ciuicis</i><br/>        <i>Molitur almas, téque tentat</i><br/>        <i>Legitimis spoliare sceptris.</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse printed in italic with long s rendered as s; some letters in the scan are worn or uncertain (e.g. "Maltare" possibly "Mactare", "Sceptra", "vasanas" possibly "vasanas"), and the initial of some lines is a decorative capital. Marks such as the small dash or mark after "Victrixque" and after "Tendit" are printing marks or damage and are not transcribed.</notes>
